                {
                    "file": "bmc_pos_mgr.cpp",
                    "line": 102,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ramesh Iyyar",
                        "email": "rameshi1@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "RameshIyyar"
                    },
                    "message": "I think we could still encounter duplicate IDs because we\u2019re relying on time, and the BMCs may not be perfectly synchronized the time (there can be slight differences at the nanosecond level while syncing though). But still, there\u2019s also a corner case where an event log is created before time synchronization occurs, which could lead to identical IDs. The likelihood is low, and we can revisit this if we start observing collisions.\n\nPlease create PEL before time sync and verify it."
                }
            ],
